{"id":"CVE-2023-46218","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2023-12-07T01:10:34.846Z","updated":"2026-10-15T00:04:49.559Z","description":"This flaw allows a malicious HTTP server to set \"super cookies\" in curl that\nare then passed back to more origins than what is otherwise allowed or\npossible. This allows a site to set cookies that then would get sent to\ndifferent and unrelated sites and domains.\n\nIt could do this by exploiting a mixed case flaw in curl's function that\nverifies a given cookie domain against the Public Suffix List (PSL). For\nexample a cookie could be set with `domain=co.UK` when the URL used a lower\ncase hostname `curl.co.uk`, even though `co.uk` is listed as a PSL domain.","cwe":["CWE-178 CWE-178 Improper Handling of Case Sensitivity"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":6.5,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"poc","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"curl","product":"curl","versions":["affected 8.4.0 <=8.4.0 (semver)","unaffected 7.46.0 <7.46.0 (semver)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.5 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIMATIC S7-1500 CPU 1518F-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.5 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"SIPLUS S7-1500 CPU 1518-4 PN/DP MFP","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected V3.1.5 <* (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"RUGGEDCOM ROX MX5000","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected 0 <V2.17.0 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"RUGGEDCOM ROX MX5000RE","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected 0 <V2.17.0 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"RUGGEDCOM ROX RX1400","defaultStatus":"unknown","versions":["affected 0 <V2.17.0 (custom)"]},{"vendor":"Siemens","product":"RUGGEDCOM ROX RX1500","defaultSt